From 7194761468c3588d1619b877a5add0d9ae2e9649 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 00:59:43 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] perf: VU0 micro programs translated like VU1's

vurecomp --vu0 translates recorded VU0 programs: a 4 KB code mask, the
VU0 interpreter for what is left (vu::interpret(0, ...)), its 256-qword
data memory (qword0), and a table of its own registered with
register_programs0 from register_generated_vu0(). They are translated
without --rz: they run on the EE thread, in round-to-nearest, as the VU0
interpreter does since the previous commit.

The runtime looks VU0 programs up by key at each VCALLMS entry, as it does
VU1's (same reachable/program_key, an entry cache of its own invalidated
by code_changed(0)); with PS2_VU_RECORD=<dir> one with no translation goes
to <dir>/vu0/.

UN5 uses two VU0 programs (eight entries with the jump targets). On the
Mac the battle replay's share of VU0 work falls from 9.1% to 0.8% of CPU
samples; the regression suite's frames are unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
